L19: Use this package for the prebuilt `AgentInterface` chat surface and default component library primitives.
L20: 
L21: ## Import
L22: 
L23:     import { AgentInterface } from "@openuidev/react-ui";
L24: ## Chat interface
L25: 
L26: `AgentInterface` is the package's chat surface — a full-page artifact chat with a thread-history sidebar, composer, and per-thread artifact workspace. It wraps `ChatProvider`, so it accepts the provider's `storage` + `llm` props alongside the shared UI props below.
L27: ### AgentInterface
L28: 
L29:     import { AgentInterface, openAIAdapter, type ChatLLM } from "@openuidev/react-ui";
L30:     import { openuiChatLibrary } from "@openuidev/react-ui/genui-lib";
L31: 
L32:     const llm: ChatLLM = {
L33:       send: ({ messages, signal }) =>
L34:         fetch("/api/chat", { method: "POST", body: JSON.stringify({ messages }), signal }),
L35:       streamProtocol: openAIAdapter(),
L36:     };
L37: 
L38:     <AgentInterface llm={llm} componentLibrary={openuiChatLibrary} />;
L39: ## Props ( AgentInterfaceProps )
L40: 
L41: `AgentInterface` extends `ChatProviderProps` (minus `children`) and adds the shared UI + theme props:
L42:   * Chat provider props (from `@openuidev/react-headless`):
L43:     * `storage?: ChatStorage` — thread (and optional artifact) persistence; defaults to in-memory
L44:     * `llm: ChatLLM` — required; `{ send({ threadId, messages, signal }), streamProtocol }`
L45:     * `artifactRenderers?: ArtifactRendererConfig[]`
L46:     * `artifactCategories?: ArtifactCategory[]`
L47:   * Shared UI props:
L48:     * `componentLibrary?: Library` (from `@openuidev/react-lang`) — drives auto-GenUI rendering
L49:     * `components?: AgentInterfaceComponents` — `{ AssistantMessage?, UserMessage? }` overrides
L50:     * `logoUrl?: string`
L51:     * `agentName?: string`
L52:     * `labels?: AgentInterfaceLabels`
L53:     * `starters?: ConversationStarterProps[]`
L54:     * `starterVariant?: ConversationStarterVariant`
L55:     * `scrollVariant?: ScrollVariant`
L56:     * `scrollOnLoad?: boolean`
L57:   * Theme wrapper props:
L58:     * `theme?: ThemeProps`
L59:     * `disableThemeProvider?: boolean`
L60: ## UI customization types
L61: 
L62: Types used by customization docs:
L63: 
L64:     type AssistantMessageComponent = React.ComponentType<{ message: AssistantMessage }>;
L65:     type UserMessageComponent = React.ComponentType<{ message: UserMessage }>;
L66: 
L67:     type ComposerProps = {
L68:       onSend: (message: string) => void;
L69:       onCancel: () => void;
L70:       isRunning: boolean;
L71:       isLoadingMessages: boolean;
L72:     };
L73:     type ComposerComponent = React.ComponentType<ComposerProps>;
L74:     type WelcomeMessageConfig =
L75:       | React.ComponentType<any>
L76:       | {
L77:           title?: string;
L78:           description?: string;
L79:           image?: { url: string } | React.ReactNode;
L80:         };
L81: 
L82:     interface ConversationStartersConfig {
L83:       variant?: "short" | "long";
L84:       options: ConversationStarterProps[];
L85:     }
L86: ## Component library exports
L87: 
L88: Two ready-to-use libraries ship with `@openuidev/react-ui`. Import from the `genui-lib` subpath:
L89: 
L90:     import {
L91:       // Chat-optimised (root = Card, includes FollowUpBlock, ListBlock, SectionBlock)
L92:       openuiChatLibrary,
L93:       openuiChatPromptOptions,
L94:       openuiChatExamples,
L95:       openuiChatAdditionalRules,
L96:       openuiChatComponentGroups,
L97:       // General-purpose (root = Stack, full component suite)
L98:       openuiLibrary,
L99:       openuiPromptOptions,
L100:       openuiExamples,
L101:       openuiAdditionalRules,
L102:       openuiComponentGroups,
L103:     } from "@openuidev/react-ui/genui-lib";
L104: 
L105: `openuiChatLibrary` — Root is `Card` (vertical, no layout params). Includes chat-specific components: `FollowUpBlock`, `ListBlock`, `SectionBlock`. Does not include `Stack`. Use with the `AgentInterface` chat surface.
L106: `openuiLibrary` — Root is `Stack`. Full layout suite with `Stack`, `Tabs`, `Carousel`, `Accordion`, `Modal`, etc. Use with the standalone `Renderer` or any non-chat layout (e.g., playground, embedded widgets, dashboards).
L107: 
L108: `openuiPromptOptions` — includes examples and additional rules for the general-purpose library. Does not include `toolExamples` — pass those in your app-level `PromptSpec` alongside tool descriptions.
L109: 
L110: Generate the system prompt at build time with the CLI:
L111: 
L112: pnpm
L113: 
L114: bun
L115: 
L116: yarn
L117: 
L118: npm
L119:     pnpx @openuidev/cli@latest generate ./src/library.ts --out src/generated/system-prompt.txt
L120: 
L121:     // Chat interface — system prompt stays on the server
L122:     <AgentInterface componentLibrary={openuiChatLibrary} ... />
L123: 
L124:     // Standalone renderer
L125:     <Renderer response={message} library={openuiLibrary} />
L126: ## Skeleton components
L127: 
L128: `Skeleton` and `TableSkeleton` are loading-state placeholders that render while data-driven genui components wait for `Query()` results. They use theme-aware CSS variables and a pulsing opacity animation.
L129: 
L130:     import { Skeleton, TableSkeleton } from "@openuidev/react-ui";
L131: ### Skeleton
L132: 
L133: A generic skeleton bar. Use standalone or with `count` for stacked bars.
L134: 
L135: Prop Type Default Description
L136: `count ``number ``1 `Number of bars to stack
L137: `height ``string``"16px"`Bar height
L138: `width ``string``"100%"`Bar width
L139: `borderRadius ``string ``undefined `Bar border radius (defaults to `--openui-radius-xs`)
L140: ### TableSkeleton
L141: 
L142: A table-shaped placeholder used by the genui `Table` component while queries load.
L143: 
L144: Prop Type Default Description
L145: `rows ``number ``5 `Number of skeleton rows
L146: `columns ``number ``4 `Number of skeleton columns
L147: 
L148: Built-in genui components like `Table` automatically render `TableSkeleton` when `useIsQueryLoading()` is `true` and no data rows exist yet.
